course: dictionary
lesson: 8949
title: Silly: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Silly is a word you already know, but it can mean different things. It can mean funny in a foolish way, or not sensible or wise, and it can be a kind thing to say to someone who is being foolish. The words around it tell you which meaning to pick. «Sharing silly jokes, like knock-knock jokes, builds friendship and helps younger children learn language.» Here silly jokes are funny, not wise.
explain: Look at the words next to silly. In «a silly mistake», silly means careless, not sensible, like adding when you should subtract. Check your meaning by putting it in place of silly: "a careless mistake" still makes sense, so you have chosen well.
explain: Silly can also be said kindly. When a friend says, «Don't be silly, you can do it!», the friend is gently telling you that you are being foolish, not being unkind. The tone and the words around it show that it is friendly.
fact: Silly is an adjective. Its forms are silly, sillier and silliest.
fact: «Silly» can mean funny in a foolish way, as in «a silly hat».
fact: «Silly» can mean not sensible or wise, as in «a silly mistake».
fact: «Silly» can be said kindly to someone who is being foolish.
fact: «Silly sayings» like FACE help you remember the notes in the spaces of music, until you just know them.
exercise: «The clown wore a silly hat and made everyone laugh.» What does silly mean here? | *Funny in a foolish way | Tired and sleepy | Very cold | Not sensible or wise
exercise: «Adding instead of subtracting was a silly mistake.» What kind of mistake is it? | A very long one | A hidden one | *A careless one, not sensible | A clever one
exercise: Ella's friend says, «Don't be silly, you can do it!» What does silly mean? | Very quiet and shy | Very loud and rude | Very sad and lonely | *Being foolish, said kindly
test: «Sharing silly jokes builds friendship.» Which word has the closest meaning to silly in this sentence? | Heavy | *Funny | Sad | Hard
test: «Silly sayings like FACE help you learn the notes in the spaces.» Which meaning of silly is used here? | Not sensible or wise | Very old | *Funny and memorable | Said kindly to a foolish friend
exam: Which sentence uses silly to mean not sensible or wise? | *That was a silly mistake to make | Sharing silly jokes is fun | I wore a silly hat to the party | Don't be silly, you are my best friend
